starDotNullT -- `*x.y` where x holds nothing refuses by name and never crashes (SEQ 301 R0, fixit starDotNull).

With the dot-chain fold the star in `*sdReq.result` binds to sdReq, which is a plain field holding no group, so opDot
is handed a NULL target. Its non-groupField arm read `target[tag]` with no guard: exit 139 and ZERO output -- born red
on trunk (measured 2026-10-05). The guard refuses by name ("opDot: the left of this dot holds nothing ..."). A refusal
ends the activation that raised it (refuse(), THE ONE FUNNEL), so sdRun's tail does not run -- SD-2x is pinned ABSENT,
and SD-3, the file's next statement, runs, with the sentinel after it. The binding of `*a.b` is NOT reopened (ruled): the spelling that works
is the temporary, SD-1 -- `blk = req.result;` then `*blk`, which reads hv.
